Maybe to clarify Dan’s erudite summary with a concrete example.
3x3 is 3^2. 3x3x3 is 3^3. 3^5 is 3x3x3x3x3 which is also 3^(3+2). But if we extend that, 3^(5+0) is also 3x3x3x3x3. So to make it work, 3^0 has to equal 1.

