However, to go further down the rabbit hole, there are plenty of scenarios where 0^0 _is_ defined to be one, so the indeterminate rule is less of a law and more of a guideline.

For example, the IEEE, Leonhard Euler, and a handful of programming languages forgo the indeterminate solution in favor of one.

